"><name><surname>Po</surname><given-names>LS</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>ZY</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsang</surname><given-names>DSC</given-names></name><name><surname>Leung</surname><given-names>LK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Baicalein and genistein display differential actions on estrogen receptor (ER) transactivation and apoptosis in MCF-7 cells</article-title><source>Cancer Lett</source><year>2002</year><volume>187</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12359348</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Powell</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Fung</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Jackson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dall'Era</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewkowicz</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith-McCune</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Aqueous extract of herb <italic>Scutellaria barbatae</italic>, a Chinese herb used for ovarian cancer, induces apoptosis of ovarian cancer cell lines</article-title><source>Gynecol Oncol</source><year>2003</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>332</fpage><lpage>340</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14599863</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ye</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Xui</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Yi</surname><given-names>JZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>DY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anticancer activity of <italic>Scutellaria baicale